_count="1" gerrit_number="414970" owner_email="pihsun@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/70/414970/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2fa97cfb1d5920ef7fadbb3f289530baeb8bb2e4" commit="c22f186c82e82df995f737b2bd82d7bf8077591f" commit_message="libcontainer: fork/exec setfiles only once for faster ARC boot  Previously, run_setfiles_command() which spawns /sbin/setfiles was called for each mount_external mount point and because of that, labeling files and directories took 800-900ms on Cyan.  With this CL, /sbin/setfiles is called only once, and the time will be like ~150ms.  BUG=b:33348324 TEST=ARC still starts  Change-Id: I2fa97cfb1d5920ef7fadbb3f289530baeb8bb2e4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/416394 Commit-Ready: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="416394" owner_email="yusukes@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/94/416394/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idf09c0304b3733d35febf698b1fc78756d6b0447" commit="2c2c0bd3389ebff5b7c45c4e3a7f54ae06fb5f39" commit_message="libcontainer: do not run setfiles for /cache  Just like /data, which libcontainer already skips, Android's /init.rc will label files and directories in /cache right after the container starts. Removing this redundant setfiles scan makes ARC faster to boot.  BUG=b:33348324 TEST=Start ARC, run &quot;find /run/containers/android_*/root/cache  -exec ls -Z {} \; | sort&quot; with and without this CL, confirm the  results are the same.  Change-Id: Idf09c0304b3733d35febf698b1fc78756